course: dictionary
lesson: 14374
title: Orderly: tidy, calm, or a helper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Orderly» comes from «order». When something is orderly, it is in order, neatly arranged. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: «The class left the hall in an orderly line for the fire drill.» Here orderly means calm and well behaved, without pushing. The sentence tells you the children were calm, not just neat.
explain: «Her desk is always orderly, with pens in one pot and books in neat piles.» Here orderly means tidy and well arranged, because the clues are pens in one pot and neat piles.
explain: «Orderly» can also be a noun. «The nurse asked the orderly to help move the bed» means a helper in a hospital, not a tidy person.
fact: «Orderly» means tidy and well arranged.
fact: «Orderly» can also mean calm and well behaved, without pushing.
fact: An «orderly» is a person who helps in a hospital, carrying things and moving patients.
fact: Check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence. Does «calm and well behaved» make sense in «an orderly line»? Yes, so it fits.
fact: The opposite of «orderly» is messy.
exercise: «Her desk is always orderly, with pens in one pot and books in neat piles.» What does orderly mean here? | Very loud | Messy and full of crumbs | Lost | *Tidy and well arranged
exercise: «The children walked to the field in an orderly line, without pushing.» What does orderly suggest? | Angry and fast | *Calm and well behaved | Wet and muddy | Hungry
exercise: In a hospital, who is an orderly? | A doctor who only works at night | A type of bed | *A helper who carries things and moves patients | A patient who is well again
test: «The orderly pushed the wheelchair down the corridor.» What is an orderly in this sentence? | *A person who helps in a hospital | A kind of bus | A wheelchair maker | A patient in the corridor
test: Which word means the opposite of orderly? | *Messy | Neat | Organised | Calm
exam: Mia says, «Please leave the room in an orderly way.» What does orderly mean here? | Loud and fast | Empty and dark | Hungry and tired | *Calm and well behaved, without pushing
